A||||1||drednot||Throttle body problems||||11||
Z||000000||drednot||05-24-2001||06:49 PM||||I found out where that ticking noise was coming from.  it is coming from the throttle body!  it is also running crappy because it is not shooting gas in all the time.  about every .5 seconds, it cuts the fuel off for a milla second.  this is where my weird engine operation /feeling like a dead cylinder is coming from.  what is the fix for this?||||reg||11
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-24-2001||06:58 PM||||If the fuel is not being sprayed in at a constant rate, see if you can listen to the fuel pump while the engine is running.  Start the car, and then press your ear to the center console and try to listen for it.  If you can hear it kick on and off, either the pump is bad or possibly the relay isnt working properly.<P>Also, what year and engine?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
